\title{An order that rests one slice at a time and places the next when that slice fills}
\description{
Only one slice is ever visible, so the size of the whole order is hidden from the book. \code{randomise_percent} varies each slice so that the pattern is harder to spot. A randomised slice is brought to the nearest whole number of lots, at least one, and a slice cancelled or rejected at the broker ends the iceberg.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
